@@s003 Kattis and Red Scare
@@s004 To be admitted to the exam you need the mandatory exercises: <b>individual exercises on Kattis</b>, corrected automatically, and a group project, <b>Red Scare</b>, in November. Without them the exam grade is NA.
@@s005 The rules
@@s006 Kattis
@@s007 9 individual exercises, corrected automatically
@@s008 Red Scare
@@s009 group project (usually 5 people) with a report, handed in on LearnIT
@@s010 Enrolment
@@s011 course on itu.kattis.com, key <code>rebelking</code> (anagram of Kleinberg); ITU email as main, real name
@@s012 Recovery
@@s013 Kattis recovery session until <b>26 November, 9:59</b>
@@s014 NCPC bonus
@@s015 at the contest of <b>3 October 2026</b>, if the team solves k &gt; 2 problems, they are worth k − 2 mandatory exercises for each member
@@s016 Already admitted?
@@s017 if you passed the mandatory part in a previous year, just write to Riko Jacob
@@s018 Two different counts
@@s019 The page "About this course" speaks of <b>10</b> mandatory items (9 Kattis + Red Scare); the official description of the course says "<b>12</b> mandatory programming assignments". Check the "Standing on Kattis" status on LearnIT, which is what counts.
